=== into itself
wbsh: mv: cannot move 'm' to a subdirectory of itself, 'm/sub'
mv m m/sub: 1
wbsh: mv: cannot move 'm' to a subdirectory of itself, 'm/sub/m'
mv m m/sub (existing): 1
wbsh: mv: cannot move 'm' to a subdirectory of itself, './m/sub/deeper'
mv m ./m/sub/deeper: 1
m still: m/a m/sub
wbsh: mv: cannot move 'm' to a subdirectory of itself, 'm/m'
mv m m: 1
wbsh: mv: 'm' and './m' are the same file
mv m .: 1
=== plain moves
mv a b: 0 -> a
into dir: 0 -> dir/b
several into dir: 0 -> dir/b dir/c dir/e
case-only rename: 0 -> S
rename dir: 0 -> new/x
=== -n -i -f -u
mv -n: 0 src=src dst=dst
prompt: mv: overwrite 'dst'? 
mv -i no: 0 src=src dst=dst
prompt: mv: overwrite 'dst'? 
mv -i yes: 0 dst=src
mv -i -f: 0 dst=src (no prompt)
mv -f -n: 0 kept src: src
mv -u older: 0 src=src dst=newer
mv -u newer: 0 dst=newest
onto read-only: 0 -> new
=== -v -t -T --
renamed 'v' -> 't/v'
renamed 't/v' -> './v'
mv -T: 0 -> tdir
wbsh: mv: cannot move 'tdir' to 'full': Directory not empty
mv -T onto non-empty dir: 1
renamed 'tdir' -> 'empty'
mv -T onto empty dir: 0
mv --: 0 -> dash
